# tests/modifiers/reset.rxt — module `modifiers` (MOD-0.5c): the `(?^)`
# construct, per the MEASURED rule in docs/dev/plan.md [MOD-0.5a] ruling 3 and
# tests/probes/probe_mod05b.c's "== (?^) reset scope per letter ==" block:
# `(?^)` resets i, m, n, s, x, xx to their HARDWIRED DEFAULTS (reset-to-
# constant, not reset-to-compile-option — the load-bearing PARSE-1 landmine)
# and does NOT touch U or J, both probed surviving.
#
# ORACLE: python `re` has no `(?^)` syntax at all (unknown extension, any
# position) — EVERY block here is `# pcre2-only`. Expectations are the
# match spans measured directly from tests/probes/probe_mod05b.c's own
# "(?^) reset scope per letter" cells (2026-08-12, libpcre2 10.46).
#
# THE J CELL IS DELIBERATELY A `perr`, NOT A MATCH/NOMATCH PIN: the
# SEMANTICS — J survives `(?^)`, i.e. `(?J)(?^)(?<g>a)(?<g>b)` still
# COMPILES and matches "ab" [0,2) — are measured against live libpcre2
# 10.46 in tests/probes/probe_mod05b.c's "(?^) reset scope per letter"
# block ("J survives ^"), but pinning that measurement as a corpus MATCH
# case needs `(?<name>...)` from module `named-groups`, which this
# milestone does not land. No block in this file may depend on a module
# MOD-0.5 doesn't ship, so instead this pins what IS true under `features
# modifiers` ALONE, in both epochs: the pattern refuses to compile, first
# because `modifiers` itself has no producer yet (today), and — once
# MOD-0.5c lands and J's own semantics are produced — because `(?<g>...)`
# then hits the `named-groups` doorway instead (verified: with
# `--features modifiers` given today, `(?J)(?^)(?<g>a)(?<g>b)` already
# refuses with "requires module 'modifiers'"; the SAME exit status is what
# every later epoch produces too, just for the later, correct reason —
# `perr` cannot distinguish the two, which is exactly why this is stable
# across the boundary this file's other blocks are not). Add the real
# match-span pin for J-survives-^ to a future corpus once `named-groups`
# has a producer; until then probe_mod05b.c is the only place that
# semantics is checked.
#
# THE D33 §9.3 RECORD: run against the MOD-0.5a-gate binary via
#   PCREC=<binary> bash tests/harness/run.sh tests/modifiers/reset.rxt
# 8 cases: 7 fail with "requires module 'modifiers'" (measured 2026-08-12).
# The J cell's `perr` already PASSES today (see above — it is satisfied by
# today's blanket gate refusal, same as the reasoning in
# malformed_and_gate.rxt) and stays passing straight through MOD-0.5c.

# ---- i is reset by (?^) --------------------------------------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?i)a(?^)a
features modifiers
m "Aa" 0 2
n "AA"

# ---- U SURVIVES (?^) — the measured exception ----------------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?U)(?^)a+
features modifiers
m "aaa" 0 1

# ---- J survives (?^) semantically (probe_mod05b.c), but that needs
# named-groups to PIN as a match case (see header) — pin only what's true
# under `features modifiers` alone: still refuses, stably, in both epochs.

pattern (?J)(?^)(?<g>a)(?<g>b)
features modifiers
perr

# ---- s is reset by (?^) ---------------------------------------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?s)(?^).
features modifiers
n "\n"

# ---- n is reset by (?^): plain (...) captures again -----------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?n)(?^)(a)
features modifiers
m "a" 0 1

# ---- x is reset by (?^): whitespace no longer skipped ---------------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)(?^)a b
features modifiers
n "ab"

# ---- xx is reset by (?^): class interior no longer touched ----------------

# pcre2-only
pattern (?xx)(?^)[a b]
features modifiers
m " " 0 1
